/**
 * parties — the schema change for one counterparty collection and two lifecycle merges.
 *
 * `payload migrate:create` has no earlier snapshot in this repository, so it emits the WHOLE schema,
 * which cannot run against a database that already has it. This migration keeps Payload's file
 * name and its two snapshots (so the next `migrate:create` diffs from here) and carries only the
 * difference between the live schema and that snapshot — every statement taken verbatim from the
 * schema Payload generated:
 *
 *   - 10 new tables: `parties` and its children, and the work-order photos
 *   - 49 tables recreated, because SQLite cannot alter a foreign key in place and their
 *     relationships now point at `parties`, or at a sales order or work order that absorbed an
 *     earlier stage
 *
 * Each table is dropped and recreated one at a time, new tables first: dropping two related tables
 * in a row fails, because the second drop still resolves the first through their shared children.
 *
 * FORWARD-ONLY. The recreated tables were empty when this was written (counted on the live
 * database), so nothing is copied across — and for the same reason there is nothing to restore.
 * The tables of the merged-away collections are left in place and unread.
 */
